# NOTE: Git LFS is intentionally NOT used for the data/models/ asset set.
#
# GitHub Pages (this site is served from the repo via "deploy from a branch")
# does NOT resolve Git LFS objects -- it serves the ~130-byte LFS POINTER text
# instead of the real binary, which breaks the .glb/.png loaders. So the full
# data/models/ asset set (geometry GLBs + perf PNG + HQ .dds textures + hero
# thumbnails + the multi-angle shots/ gallery) is committed as PLAIN git blobs
# that Pages serves correctly. (GitHub Pages documents a 1 GB published-site
# limit, but it isn't strictly enforced here -- the full set serves fine.)
